<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Oct 7.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Oct 7.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Oct 7</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   230	   0.49     466350 107.26    11.11</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   169	   0.31     330900  55.92     9.56</p>
<p>Reliance	     190	   0.34     195200  37.09     9.33</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    220	   0.44     130550  28.72    10.43</p>
<p>ACC		   1680	   2.83	16630  27.94     8.78</p>
<p>Tata Power	   118	   0.23     220600  26.03    10.16</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    393	   0.76	48600  19.10    10.08</p>
<p>BSES Ltd	     164	   0.29	98600  16.17     9.22</p>
<p>IPCL		   111	   0.13	93700  10.40     6.11</p>
<p>ICICI		   67	   0.07     138900   9.31     5.45</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to  9.70  percent on an annualised basis against 13.70 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Sept 28. -- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
